}

.jam_banner_outer .jam_banner{
border-top: 4px solid var(--accent);  
border-bottom: 4px solid var(--accent);
  box-shadow:
    0 22px 50px rgba(0,0,0,0.46),
    0 0 0 5px rgba(8, 6, 10, 0.88),
    0 0 18px rgba(241, 196, 107, 0.08);
  transition: transform 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease, filter 0.25s ease;

}

.jam_banner_outer .jam_banner:hover{
  filter: brightness(1.02) saturate(1.01);
  box-shadow:
    0 26px 54px rgba(0,0,0,0.50),
    0 0 0 5px rgba(8, 6, 10, 0.88),
    0 0 18px rgba(241, 196, 107, 0.12);
}

.custom-rules{
  background:
    linear-gradient(to bottom,
      rgba(201, 58, 47, 0.06),
      rgba(241, 196, 107, 0.03));
  border: 1px solid var(--border2);
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 6px;
}

.custom-rulesummary{
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  background:
    linear-gradient(135deg,
      rgba(22, 12, 18, 0.98),
      rgba(44, 16, 18, 0.96));
  color: var(--paper);
  padding: 15px;
  margin: 14px 0 0 0;
  border-radius: 12px;
  font-size: 1.05em;
}

summary{
  border: 1px solid var(--border2);
  cursor: pointer;
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 10px 12px;
  margin: 10px 0 0 0;
  background:
    linear-gradient(to right,
      rgba(66, 18, 22, 0.45),
      rgba(14, 10, 14, 0.72));
  color: var(--paper);
}

summary:hover{
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
}

details > summary{
  list-style: none;
  position: relative;
  padding-left: 42px;
}

details > summary::before{
  content: "💣";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  width: 28px;
  height: 28px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 2px solid var(--border);

  background: var(--accent);
  box-shadow:
    0 0 8px rgba(241,196,107,0.15),
    inset 0 0 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);

  font-size: 2.5em;
}

details[open] > summary::before{
  content: "💥";
  background: var(--ink);
  box-shadow:
    0 0 12px rgba(241,196,107,0.25),
    inset 0 0 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
}

.custom-devtalk{
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0;
  right: 20px;
  width: 15vw;
  max-height: 22vh;
  overflow: hidden;
  z-index: 999;
  background:
    linear-gradient(to bottom,
      rgba(64, 14, 20, 0.98),
      rgba(12, 8, 12, 0.98));
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 24px 24px 10px 10px;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 1.2em;
  color: var(--paper);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow), var(--glow);
}

.button,
input[type="submit"],
button{
  border-radius: 999px;
  border: 2px solid rgba(59, 31, 12, 0.92);
  background:
    linear-gradient(to bottom,
      #f7dda0,
      #e7bd64 55%,
      #c68432 100%);
  color: var(--ink);
  box-shadow:
    0 8px 18px rgba(0,0,0,0.34),
    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.22);
} </style></head><body class="locale_en jam_layout_widget layout_widget no_theme_toggle responsive" data-host="itch.io" data-page_name="view_jam"><div class="gray jam_layout_header_widget header_widget base_widget small_logo" id="jam_layout_header_9637592"><a class="skip_to_main" href="#maincontent">Skip to main content</a><div class="primary_header"><h1 title="itch.io - indie game hosting marketplace" class="title"><a class="header_logo" title="itch.io - indie game hosting marketplace" href="/"><span class="visually_hidden">itch.io</span><img class="full_logo" alt="itch.io logo &amp; title" src="https://static.itch.io/images/logo-black-new.svg" height="199" width="775"/><img class="minimal_logo" alt="itch.io logo" src="https://static.itch.io/images/itchio-textless-black.svg" height="235" width="262"/></a></h1><div class="header_buttons"><a class="header_button browse_btn" data-label="browse" href="/games">Browse Games</a><a class="header_button jams_btn" data-label="jams" href="/jams">Game Jams</a><a class="header_button developers_btn" data-label="developers" href="/developers"><span aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-upload"></span>Upload Game</a><a class="header_button devlogs_btn" data-label="devlogs" href="/devlogs">Developer Logs</a><a class="header_button community.home_btn" data-label="community.home" href="/community">Community</a></div><form class="game_search" action="/search"><input required="required" class="search_input" type="text" name="q" placeholder="Search for games, jams, tags or creators"/><button aria-label="Search" class="submit_btn"><svg role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden stroke-linejoin="round" stroke="currentColor" fill="none" class="svgicon icon_search" version="1.1"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line></svg></button></form><div class="user_panel_widget base_widget" id="user_panel_2965227"><a data-label="log_in" data-register_action="header" class="panel_button" href="/login">Log in</a><a data-label="register" data-register_action="header" class="panel_button register_button" href="/register">Register</a></div></div><div class="header_dropdown" data-target="browse"><a href="/games/store">Indie game store</a><a href="/games/free">Free games</a><a href="/games/fun">Fun games</a><a href="/games/tag-horror">Horror games</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/tools">Game development</a><a href="/game-assets">Assets</a><a href="/comics">Comics</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/sales">Sales</a><a href="/bundles">Bundles</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/jobs">Jobs</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/tags">Tags</a><a href="/game-development/engines">Game Engines</a></div></div><div class="jam_page_wrap" id="wrapper"><div class="view_jam_page view_jam_base_page page_widget base_widget view_jam_default during_submit has_banner" id="view_jam_718751"><div class="jam_banner_outer"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1hZ2UyL2phbS80MTQ0NTMvMjYzMDQyNTUucG5n/original/1vQwk3.png" class="jam_banner full_width"/></div><div class="jam_body"><div class="jam_header_widget base_widget" id="jam_header_830592"><div class="header_inner"><div class="header_columns"><div class="title_colum"><h1 class="jam_title_header"><a href="/jam/cgdct-jam-2026">Cute Girls Doing Cool Things VN Jam 2026</a></h1><div class="jam_host_header">Hosted by <a href="https://aiainaine.itch.io">aine</a>, <a href="https://cuteshadow.itch.io">CuteShadow</a>, <a href="https://makevisualnovels.itch.io">Stella @ MakeVisualNovels</a> · <a href="https://bsky.app/hashtag/CGDCTJam">#CGDCTJam</a></div></div><div class="stats_container"><div class="stat_box"><div class="stat_value">288</div><div class="stat_label">Joined</div></div><div class="stat_box"><a href="/jam/cgdct-jam-2026/entries"><div class="stat_value">12</div><div class="stat_label">Entries</div></a></div></div></div><div class="header_tabs"><a class="header_tab active" data-label="tab_view_jam" href="/jam/cgdct-jam-2026">Overview</a><a class="header_tab" data-label="tab_view_jam_entries" href="/jam/cgdct-jam-2026/entries">Submissions</a><div class="tab_group"><a class="header_tab" href="/jam/cgdct-jam-2026/community">Community</a><span class="community_activity">29</span></div><a class="header_tab" data-label="tab_view_jam_feed" href="/jam/cgdct-jam-2026/feed">Submission feed</a></div></div></div><div class="submitter_outer"><div class="jam_submitter_widget base_widget during_submit" id="jam_submitter_323286"><div class="date_data">Submissions open from <span data-format="MMMM Do YYYY [at] h:mm A" class="date_format">2026-06-01 04:00:00</span> to <span data-format="MMMM Do YYYY [at] h:mm A" class="date_format">2026-08-03 04:00:00</span></div><div class="countdown"><span class="countdown_label">Submissions due in</span><div class="times"><div data-name="years" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">years</div></div><div data-name="months" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">months</div></div><div data-name="days" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">days</div></div><div data-name="hours" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">hours</div></div><div data-name="minutes" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">minutes</div></div><div data-name="seconds" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">seconds</div></div></div></div><div class="state_action"><button class="button fat submitter_button join_jam_btn" data-href="/jam/414453/join" data-method="post">Join jam</button></div></div></div><div class="jam_content user_formatted"><h1 class="text-center">Cute Girls Doing Cool Things</h1>
<h3 class="text-center"><em>&quot;Summer’s here! You’ve got 2 months to create the ultimate summer blockbuster visual novel&hellip; starring cute girls?!&quot;</em></h3>
<p class="text-center">Banner art by&nbsp;<a href="https://x.com/neoqh0st?s=21" target="_blank" referrerpolicy="origin" rel="nofollow noopener">Neo</a>.
</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<div class="custom-theme"><p>Permanent Theme:</p>
<h2 class="custom-header">Summer Blockbuster</h2>
<h2 class="text-center">ft. Cute Girls</h2>
</div>
<p class="text-justify">Summer blockbusters are big-budget films known for fast action, famous stars, and breathtaking special effects. They&#x27;re released during the summer, when families have more free time and cinemas can sell more seats.&nbsp;Some prompts you could see in a summer blockbuster include, but are not limited to:</p>
<ul class="text-justify"><li class="text-justify"><strong>Crime &amp; Heists:</strong>&nbsp;secret agents or spies, bank or casino heists, cops and robbers, hackers, treasure hunting&nbsp;
</li><li class="text-justify"><strong>Worldwide Catastrophes:</strong>&nbsp;zombie apocalypse, alien invasion, saving the world
</li><li class="text-justify"><strong>Intense Action:</strong>&nbsp;car chases, martial arts or gunfights, big explosions
</li><li class="text-justify">and so much more...</li></ul>
<p class="text-justify">Now, who better to star in these high-stakes scenarios than a cast of cute girls? The fun lies in the contrast between the danger and the adorable moe designs. They can be badass one moment and silly the next, highlighting both their cool and cute sides.</p>
<p><br></p>
<h2 class="custom-header">Rules</h2>
<p class="text-center">(click for more details)</p>
<div class="custom-rules">
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Submissions must be visual novels.</strong></summary>
    <p>VN hybrids are also allowed as long as the main game is identifiable as a visual novel. Please consider the narrative relevance before adding any minigames, and accessibility options to make them easier or skippable (e.g. Story Mode).</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Submissions must be made in their entirety between the jam&#x27;s running period of June 1st–August 3rd.</strong></summary>
    <p>You are permitted to create concept art, written outlines, and build teams prior to the start date.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Tag your game with content warnings appropriately.</strong></summary>
    <p>Spoilers aren&#x27;t an excuse. Let players know what they&#x27;re getting into, especially any sensitive content.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Include a thumbnail, and screenshots on your game page.</strong></summary>
    <p>Show players a preview of what they&#x27;re getting into, and confidence that what they&#x27;re downloading is a visual novel and not a virus or spam.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>No sexual content, gore or self-harm.</strong></summary>
    <p>This type of content doesn&#x27;t fit the mass-appeal vibes of the theme. Keep it fun for the whole (rhetorical)&nbsp;family!</p>
    <p>Death, blood, and violence are acceptable as long as it&#x27;s not too graphic. If it can be shown in theatres or be livestreamed, then you&#x27;re good.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Pre-existing resources are permitted as long as they are also available for usage/purchase by all other participants at the time the jam starts.</strong></summary>
    <p>You are welcome to use&nbsp;pre-existing, pre-packaged assets to help supplement your development to ease the burdens of skill and time.</p>
    <p>If these are resources you have personally made, they must be publicly&nbsp;available at least 30 days prior to the start of the jam.&nbsp;</p><p>For example, if you make generic tools and assets for the community, of course you can use them in your own project. Just don&#x27;t try to be cheeky and pre-release a mechanic or assets you fully intend to use specifically for your submission.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>No generative AI usage in any aspect of your project.</strong></summary>
    <p>Humans must illustrate, write, program, etc. every part of your submission! This includes pre-production: outlining, brainstorming, and art referencing.</p><p>Be mindful if you are using third party assets as per the previous rule, as this extends to 3rd party assets. Check your sources!</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Your jam submissions must be made freely available during the month of August!</strong>&nbsp;</summary><p>Let&#x27;s keep the submissions available for everyone during the rating period! You&#x27;re welcome to charge for your submissions later.</p></details></div>
<h2 class="custom-header">FAQ</h2>
<div class="custom-rules">
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Do all my characters have to be girls?</strong></summary>
    <p>You can include non-girl characters, as long as the main cast consists of cute girls. There are no restrictions on who can identify as a girl or what that word means to you, as long as you&#x27;re&nbsp;being sincere.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>What does CGDCT stand for?</strong></summary>
    <p>CGDCT is usually short for <a target="_blank" href="https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CuteGirlsDoingCuteThings" referrerpolicy="origin" rel="nofollow noopener">Cute Girls Doing Cute Things</a>, but this jam follows the <a target="_blank" href="https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RuleOfCool" referrerpolicy="origin" rel="nofollow noopener">Rule of Cute</a>; anything is cute as long as cute girls are doing it (even if it involves loading heavy artillery), so we changed the second “Cute” to “Cool”.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Can I include dark, mature themes and settings?</strong></summary>
    <p>Making your girls suffer in a cruel, brutal world is part of the fun, but it should have a relatively hopeful message in the end, even if sacrifices had to be made along the way. Cuteness must prevail.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Can I submit demos and WIPs?</strong></summary>
    <p>You can, but aim to make something you can finish during the jam. Try not to crunch or overscope.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary><strong>Can I make a fangame of an existing IP?</strong></summary><p>Fangames are new, standalone&nbsp;renditions of existing worlds and characters built&nbsp;from scratch.&nbsp;Note that, due to general inaccessibility, ripping raw assets from&nbsp;the original media is not allowed.<br></p><p>IP law is complicated, and we don&#x27;t want you risking getting into legal trouble.&nbsp;You must follow the official IP Guidelines for fangames of your chosen IP or you cannot submit it to this jam.</p>
    <blockquote>For example, Doki Doki Literature Club has <a target="_blank" href="https://teamsalvato.com/ip-guidelines" referrerpolicy="origin" rel="nofollow noopener">official guidelines</a> for fan content and you must follow them if you wished to submit a DDLC fangame.</blockquote></details></div>
